# Local tmux config (copied from sample)
tmux.conf
# All nine subrepos are imported, so no `/name/` entry survives here for the eight
# whose directories are gone. The rule that governed them is kept as a warning:
# ANCHOR any such entry (`/name/`, not `name`) — an unanchored name matches a
# directory at ANY depth, so a bare `tempest` also swallowed
# reference/atari-source/tempest/ and 57 files of vendored ROM source vanished
# from `git add` without a word.
#
# LEFTOVER, not a subrepo. arcade-shared's content was imported to src/shared/
# (13 .ts files in each, the same library), but the original directory was never
# deleted — the teardown task owns that. Until then it sits here as 59M of stale
# library plus its own node_modules/ and dist/, matched by nothing.
#
# Ignored because the only thing that was stopping `git add -A` from committing
# all 59M was a rule people have to remember. That is the same gap /dist/ below
# was added to close, and this epic has repeatedly found that a guarantee resting
# on discipline rather than mechanism is the one that eventually fails.
#
# Delete this line together with the directory.
/arcade-shared/
out/audio/
# Build output. Every app now builds into a ROOT dist/<id>/ (dist/ itself for the
# lobby) via `node scripts/build-app.mjs <id>`. Each subrepo used to carry its own
# `dist/` rule in its own .gitignore; those left with the per-repo tooling, so
# until this line existed nothing ignored the build at all and a single
# `git add -A` would have committed eight built applications.
#
# ANCHORED (`/dist/`, not `dist/`) per the warning above: the build output is one
# specific directory at the root, and an unanchored rule would also swallow any
# directory named dist at ANY depth — including vendored reference material.
/dist/
# Imported subrepos' own .git directories, parked here rather than deleted so the
# pre-monorepo history stays recoverable on this machine. Safe to remove once every
# game is imported and its GitHub remote is confirmed in sync.
.migration-backup/
# Persona portrait art — GENERATED OUTPUT, not source. `just portraits <theme>`
# renders it (GPU, and `portraits-all` covers 102 themes), tmux displays it inline
# via the Kitty/iTerm2/Sixel passthrough, and `pf init` drops a prebuilt copy in.
# 5.9MB of images that no build, suite or sprint command consumes, all of it
# reproducible — ignored rather than deleted, since the next `pf init` restores it.
.pennyfarthing/personas/portraits/
